(684,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","No, John. You do not write better than AI ever will. At some point, perhaps in two years, perhaps in seven, AI will be better at writing than you are.","Raw live page. Original is Quill's own comment, 'February 15, 2026, 1:01 am'; Fatman re-quotes it verbatim at 9:50 am, so the claim's 'quoted by another commenter' also holds. Note the page hedges ('At some point, perhaps in two years, perhaps in seven'); the claim's 'within roughly two to seven years' is a fair but slightly tighter rendering."),
(685,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","It is you giving it the parameters of a block of text, and saying, 'Fill this space with the shape of the thing I'm asking about.' It will conjure not an answer, but an answer-shaped thing.","Live URL soft-404s to the site homepage for non-browser clients (HTTP 200 but wrong document; a nonsense slug returns the same page). Verified on the Wayback raw capture 20260618213915id_ and confirmed identical in captures 20250524060542id_ and 20250530191023id_. Quote exact; both limbs in consecutive sentences."),
(686,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","It is, almost literally, a super-fancy lorum ipsum generator.","Wayback raw captures (three, identical). Quote exact including the post's own misspelling 'lorum', and 'almost literally' is Wendig's own wording."),
(687,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","The paragraphs have words, sometimes big words, and lots of sentences, but they frequently say nothing.","Wayback raw captures. Comment byline 'bluespiderwort says:' timestamped 'May 21, 2025 - 6:51 PM' on that post's thread. Quote exact; the full sentence carries the 'lots of sentences, but frequently say nothing' limb."),
(688,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","Paragraphs into my nascent mystery, it had no idea what was happening; or at least, not enough of an idea to 'participate' in any meaningful way.","Raw live page (robinsloan.com, HTTP 200). Quote exact. Supporting limbs on the same page: the story was 'commissioned by Google and produced using a new AI-powered editor called Wordcraft'; Sloan 'liked the idea of giving the AI the role of the detective' in 'some kind of locked-room mystery'."),
(689,"VERIFIED_VERBATIM","It knew I was writing a mystery; it reached for the appropriate terms and tropes; but that wasn't anywhere close to being sufficient.","Raw live page. Quote exact and every limb of the claim is in this single sentence."),
